cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the results, please cite the paper."
title: "Characterizing and mitigating the in-context cliff: a complementary learning systems perspective on fast and slow learning in large language models"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible measurements and analyses of many-shot classification, common-prompt
  likelihood and output compliance, released post-training stages, count/length
  controls, state transfer and regional adaptation. All completed final outcomes
  are retained, including null and adverse results. Whole-prompt regional adaptation
  can damage zero-shot output compliance and does not localize the original deficit.
  Contextual query-label training is evaluated separately from whole-prompt training.
version: 2.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Rostami
    given-names: Mohammad
repository-code: "https://github.com/anomsubmission/LLM_Context_Collapse"
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - in-context learning
  - complementary learning systems
  - many-shot prompting
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - continual learning
